reviewNotes:
Substrate Sync is a client for Substrate, a personal server its user runs; the app does nothing without one. We run a demonstration server for review with no real user's data.

To sign in:
1. Open the app. Under Repository or server, enter {server} and tap Continue.
2. Tap Sign In with Your Substrate.
3. On the server's Sign in to your Substrate page, enter the repository and password below and tap Sign in.
4. Scroll down and tap Approve and set up (Approve, once the app is set up). The app returns signed in.

Repository: {user}
Password: {password}

Health, Contacts, Calendar and Reminders are on by default and each asks for its system permission at setup; each can be turned off. Places is off until turned on. Places uses visit monitoring under Always location access, only to record where the device stayed; it uses no continuous location background mode. Data goes only to the user's own server and is never used for advertising. Accounts live on the user's own server and are never created in the app. Privacy policy: {privacy}
